"""A source-comment and line-marker detector, not a full code parser.

Comment punctuation (#, //, -- and %) receives a negative response when
it starts a line. Indentation, backtick quoting, escaped newlines, and
recent code syntax strengthen it. Headings, bullets and tabbed spacing
receive weaker responses; ordinary tokens receive zero. Context is only
the previous 500 characters and is reset at document boundaries.
